% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% the words of sellers for jewellery, gems, metals, wigs and hair, and
% artificial flowers, in the words of the tariff (Chapters 67 and 71). Each
% word cites the text that says what it means: the tariff's headings and
% notes, the Federal Trade Commission's Jewelry Guides (16 CFR Part 23: what
% "sterling", "14K", "gold filled", "cultured pearl", "diamond" may mean on a
% product sold in the United States), US Customs rulings, and the description
% of the listings' fields (sources/listings/
% marketplace_fields_jewellery_wigs_flowers.txt) for what a field means.
% Bridges.
%
% Left out, because no saved text says what the word means for the tariff:
%   - "zircon" (a natural stone, or a seller's word for cubic zirconia?),
%     "moissanite", "moon stone" — no ruling or guide names them;
%   - "pearl" and "freshwater pearl" unqualified: the FTC guide forbids
%     "pearl" for a cultured or an imitation pearl, but marketplace sellers
%     use it for imitation pearls, and a mistake moves the good between 7116
%     and 7117 (US Customs, NY N005326, classifies "fresh water pearl
%     jewelry" one way "if of natural pearls" and another "if of cultured");
%   - "silver" and "gold" unqualified: the FTC guide forbids the unqualified
%     word "silver", and both name a colour as often as a metal; "alloy";
%   - plating ("gold plated", "silver plated", "rhodium plated"): note 6,
%     plating is not precious metal; the body metal decides;
%   - "charms", "beads", "jewelry findings": a charm, a bead or a finding is
%     no article of jewelry of note 9 by itself; US Customs classifies
%     plastic charms and beads in 3926 (uses background) and charms on a
%     necklace in 7117 — the word does not decide;
%   - "hair bundles", "human hair weave", "remy hair": no text; a bare
%     "rose" (a live rose is of Chapter 6); "Fine or Fashion".
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a thing* names the material *a name*; undefined.
    *a name* is a word for the kind *a kind*.
    *a field* is a field that names the kind.
    *a field* is a field of the kind *a kind*.
    *a name* is a word for the metal *a metal*.
    *a name* is a word for cladding with *a metal*.
    *a field* is a field that names the metal.
    *a name* is a word for the gem *a gem*.
    *a field* is a field that names the gem.
    *a name* is a word for the hair *a hair*.
    *a field* is a field of human hair.
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.
    the metal of *a thing* is *a metal*.
    *a thing* is clad with *a metal*.
    the gem of *a thing* is *a gem*.
    the hair of *a thing* is *a hair*.

